## STEP 12 — ASSESS WHETHER CONTINUOUS EFFECT-MODIFICATION MODELING IS PLAUSIBLE

Without using outcomes, classify feasibility as:

### GOOD
Both treatments have meaningful representation across most of the ALBI continuum and weighted balance is adequate.

### LIMITED
A continuous interaction may be estimable only over a restricted common-support interval.

### POOR
One treatment is too sparse across clinically important ALBI regions for credible continuous interaction modeling.

Base this on:
- ALBI counts/density
- propensity support
- effective sample size
- baseline balance

Do not base it on outcome significance.

